To achieve O(1) for both get and put, I need a combination of a hash map (unordered_map) and a doubly linked list.
- The hash map stores the key and an iterator to the node in the doubly linked list. This allows O(1) lookup by key.
- The doubly linked list maintains the order of usage. The most recently used items are at the front (or back), and the least recently used items are at the back (or front).
- When a key is accessed (get) or inserted/updated (put), the corresponding node is moved to the front of the list.
- When the cache is full and a new item needs to be inserted, the node at the back of the list (LRU) is removed, and the new node is added to the front.

